From b4b8699d51ada399b275d123228ac5602891450c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Jones <grahamjonesgs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 11:16:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add KlaussCPU target support (minimal, via JSON target
 spec)

- callconv: new klausscpu module mirroring clang's DefaultABIInfo
  (scalars direct + extended to 64-bit, aggregates indirect, i128
  direct/legalizer-split), dispatched via Arch::Other("klausscpu")
  guard so no Arch enum variant or exhaustive-match churn is needed.
- rustc_llvm: register the klausscpu LLVM component and its five
  LLVMInitializeKlaussCPU* entry points.

Target spec ships as JSON next to the backend in the klausscpu-llvm
fork (llvm/lib/Target/KlaussCPU/rust/klausscpu-unknown-none-elf.json);
arch strings unknown to rustc parse as Arch::Other, which flows through
desc_symbol/object-arch already.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
